{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The sons of Jer[Bb]ahmeel are told
From Hez[Eb]ron’s firstborn line
[Bb]Ram, Bu[Gm7]nah, Oren, [F]Ozem
And A[Eb]hijah shine
Anoth[Bb]er wife [Gm7]was Atarah
She [Bb/D]bore the son [Eb]Onam
Shammai [Bb]and [Gm7]Jada followed
[Bb/D]Through the years [Eb]to come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Sheshan [Bb]had no sons, only daughters
He gave his child a[Eb]way
To Jarha, his [Bb]Egyp[Gm7]tian servant
In that [Bbmaj7/F]simple day
[Eb]Attai came from that [Bb]union
Nathan, then Z[Bb/D]abad
[Eb]Ephlal and Obed [Bb]followed
In the [Bb/D]written re[Eb]cord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Eleasah fa[Bb]thered Sismai
Sismai fathered [F]Shallum
[Gm]Shallum fathered Je[Eb]kamiah
[Bb]Jekamiah fa[F]thered Elis[Eb]hama
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Obed fathered Jehu, [Bb]sure
Jehu fathered A[Bb/D]zariah
Aza[Eb]riah fathered Helez
[Bb]He[Gm]lez fathered Elea[Bbmaj7/F]sah
The names [Eb]are kept in the book
[Bb]For Israel’s memo[Bb/D]ry
Trib[Eb]al identity [Bb]preserved
In the [Bb/D]family tree
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Elea[Eb]sah fathered Sis[Bb]mai
Sismai fathered Shal[F]lum
[Gm]Shallum fathered Je[Eb]kamiah
[Bb]Jekamiah fathered [F]Elisha[Eb]ma
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
God’s faithfulness holds the [Bb]line
Through generations of [Bb/D]men
The royal [Eb]blood of Ju[Bb]dah
En[Gm]dures until the [Bb/F]end
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
E[Eb]leasah fathered Sis[Bb]mai
Sismai fathered Shal[F]lum
[Gm]Shallum fathered Je[Eb]kamiah
